{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he said: YHWH will roar</b> — a great thunder that will be, and then the rain will be withheld, and there will be a lack of bread and water for them, as he will mention. Or the meaning is that this prophet heard the voice of HaShem by way of prophecy, a great voice like the roar of a lion, and behold the voice is like a decree decreed from HaShem; therefore he said: <b>and the pastures of the shepherds mourn</b>, for the sheep will die without a shepherd." "<b>and the top of Carmel dries up</b> — the trees seen at the top. And the one who explains <b>pastures of the shepherds</b> as referring to kings — it is not according to the sense of the pericope."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:17:43.208931169Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}